WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.228 --> 00:00:11.814
The sun sets.

2
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:16.057
Wolves howl at the rising moon.

3
00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:20.280
Owls' hoots echo through the night.

4
00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:25.564
Bats swoop through the darkness on silent wings.

5
00:00:26.464 --> 00:00:31.668
These creatures of the night are the stuff of spooky legends—and scary movies.

6
00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.922
But is there any truth to the legends surrounding these animals?

7
00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:40.944
Long ago it was frightening to hear wolves howling at night.

8
00:00:42.445 --> 00:00:48.268
Wolves were seen as dangerous beasts, and people who did horrible things were thought of as beasts.

9
00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:56.292
So legends arose of werewolves—people who turned into wolf-like beasts during a full moon.

10
00:00:58.752 --> 00:01:03.014
These werewolves had sharp fangs and claws and hairy bodies.

11
00:01:04.735 --> 00:01:11.098
They remained vicious beasts until the sun rose, when they returned to their human forms and personalities.

12
00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:21.222
Today we know that werewolves aren't real.

13
00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:25.184
We also know that wolves don't howl at night to be scary.

14
00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:28.638
Wolves are nocturnal, so they're awake at night.

15
00:01:30.059 --> 00:01:33.882
They howl to communicate with their pack or stake out territory.

16
00:01:35.403 --> 00:01:41.888
Pointing their noses toward the sky helps their sounds carry for a long distance—9 to 16 kilometers.

17
00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:47.092
Despite the legends, wolves don't howl more during full moons.

18
00:01:48.313 --> 00:01:51.756
People were just more likely to see wolves under the light of a full moon!

19
00:01:53.492 --> 00:01:57.255
The hoot of the owl also struck terror in people long ago.

20
00:01:58.436 --> 00:02:03.159
As with wolves, spooky legends arose about these mysterious nighttime creatures.

21
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.763
In some legends witches turned into owls at night.

22
00:02:08.903 --> 00:02:11.565
Many cultures saw owls as a symbol of death.

23
00:02:12.986 --> 00:02:18.050
In Europe, for example, people believed that an owl nearby meant someone would die.

24
00:02:19.111 --> 00:02:23.486
When they heard the owl hoot, they hoped its big shiny eyes were not watching them!

25
00:02:25.247 --> 00:02:28.710
Luckily owls don't hoot at night as messengers of doom.

26
00:02:30.411 --> 00:02:32.693
Owls, like wolves, are nocturnal.

27
00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:36.515
They hoot to communicate with other owls.

28
00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:42.460
They may hoot to claim territory or talk to a mate or their chicks.

29
00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:46.022
Sometimes their hoots are warnings.

30
00:02:46.763 --> 00:02:48.284
But these aren't warnings of death.

31
00:02:49.344 --> 00:02:52.807
These warning hoots let other owls know there are people nearby!

32
00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.493
Why do owls have such large eyes that glow in the darkness?

33
00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:05.217
Since owls hunt at night, their eyes help them see.

34
00:03:06.618 --> 00:03:09.661
Owls can also turn their necks so they can see backwards.

35
00:03:10.962 --> 00:03:13.304
This helps them silently track their prey.

36
00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:22.284
Another creature of legend is the vampire bat—the strange flying mammal that sucks blood.

37
00:03:23.444 --> 00:03:27.427
Surprisingly, legends about vampires didn't come from vampire bats.

38
00:03:28.668 --> 00:03:34.391
People from Ancient Egypt, Tibet, and Rome had stories about vampires who sucked blood.

39
00:03:35.952 --> 00:03:42.296
Much later, European explorers discovered bats in Mexico and Central America that lived off blood.

40
00:03:43.872 --> 00:03:47.733
They named these bats vampire bats after the legendary creatures.

41
00:03:49.874 --> 00:03:54.475
The legend about human vampires turning into vampire bats began even later.

42
00:03:56.256 --> 00:03:59.877
That legend is from Dracula, the famous horror novel.

43
00:04:01.357 --> 00:04:05.478
The character Dracula could turn into a bat and fly through the night.

44
00:04:06.598 --> 00:04:10.820
But unlike vampires from legends, vampire bats don't really suck blood.

45
00:04:12.424 --> 00:04:15.787
Vampire bats usually approach their targets from the ground.

46
00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.572
They use their sharp teeth to pierce the skin of their prey.

47
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:27.015
Then they drink the flowing blood using their tongues.

48
00:04:28.416 --> 00:04:31.579
They don't kill their victims—or turn them into vampires!

49
00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:34.941
And vampire bats rarely prey on humans.

50
00:04:35.922 --> 00:04:38.244
They usually feed on cattle and horses.

51
00:04:39.592 --> 00:04:42.215
People have always tried to explain the unknown.

52
00:04:43.376 --> 00:04:46.779
Legends help to explain mysterious things that people encounter.

53
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.784
Now we know that some legends aren't true, but people still enjoy a good scary story.

54
00:04:54.325 --> 00:05:00.211
When the moon rises, filling the night with shadows, it's fun to pretend legends are real!
